        misreading: 'An alpha of .98 shows that the scale measures one thing.',
        truth: 'Items that tap several unrelated traits can still produce a high alpha (Rodriguez et al., 2016b). Alpha blends the strength of the general factor with that of the group factors (Zinbarg et al., 2005). On the MASC, alpha and omega are both .98. Only ω<sub>H</sub> shows how much of that is general anxiety.',
